@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, relations: [x.code/touches, x.code/exercises] }

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: Cargo.toml@1693fc23e399 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "rust-version = \"1.86\"" }
~ Set MSRV to Rust 1.86

To ensure compatibility with dependencies that require newer versions of Rust.

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: Cargo.toml@1693fc23e399 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "homepage     = \"https://github.com/vulogov/rust_smysl\"\nkeywords     = [\"cargo-subcommand\", \"rationale\", \"provenance\", \"smysl\", \"decisions\"]\ncategories   = [\"development-tools::cargo-plugins\", \"development-tools\"]" }
~ Add homepage, keywords, categories, and README to each crate

To provide necessary metadata for crates.io listing and discovery.

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:1693fc23e3997eb01b88315032c1d3ccda675b7f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "crates.io resolves path dependencies by version, so git, facts and corpus go first, then bench and extract, then verdict and evidence, then the subcommand." }
~ Publish eight crates in a specific order

To ensure path dependencies are resolved correctly by crates.io.

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:1693fc23e3997eb01b88315032c1d3ccda675b7f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`cargo-smysl` keeps its own keywords rather than the workspace's: it is the crate people install, and they find it by searching for a cargo subcommand." }
~ Keep `cargo-smysl` keywords separate from the workspace

`cargo-smysl` is the crate people install via search for a cargo subcommand.

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:1693fc23e3997eb01b88315032c1d3ccda675b7f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It also records what to be sure of before publishing, since a version can be yanked but never removed, and a crate name is claimed on first publish." }
~ Document the release process in `docs/releasing.md`

To provide clear instructions for maintaining and publishing the project.

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:1693fc23e3997eb01b88315032c1d3ccda675b7f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Eight crates publish; the evaluation tooling does not, and says so." }
~ Exclude `cargo-smysl-eval` from publication

`cargo-smysl-eval` is evaluation tooling that reads files outside its own package.

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-git/Cargo.toml@1693fc23e399 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "# Model-free and self-contained (plan §1): git objects are read with gix, never by running `git`." }
~ Use `gix` for reading git objects instead of running `git`

To ensure self-contained operation without relying on external binaries.

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: Cargo.toml@1693fc23e399 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "cargo-smysl-corpus   = { path = \"crates/cargo-smysl-corpus\",   version = \"0.2.0-dev\" }" }
~ Pin dependencies to specific versions in the workspace

To maintain consistency across all crates in the workspace.

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-extract/Cargo.toml@1693fc23e399 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "# Hosted providers need TLS; the default build has no network stack at all (D18)." }
~ Add `hosted` feature to some crates for optional TLS support

To provide flexibility in network requirements.

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/Cargo.toml@1693fc23e399 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "# Label and adjudication files are TOML: a person edits them by hand, so they are not JSON." }
~ Use `serde_json` and `toml` for configuration files

To support human-editable configuration files.

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:1693fc23e3997eb01b88315032c1d3ccda675b7f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "A published package cannot reach outside itself, so the crate-level README is short and the full documentation stays in the repository." }
~ Include `README.md` in each crate for crates.io listing

To provide brief descriptions for each crate on crates.io.

@decision d/g1693fc23e399-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:1693fc23e3997eb01b88315032c1d3ccda675b7f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`cargo package` fails for everything past wave one until wave one is on crates.io — expected, and written down so it is not mistaken for a fault." }
~ Document the expected behavior of `cargo package` before first publish

To clarify expectations for developers during the release process.

